From f9d6392a590bce30309e45ca4b499bb36fd55548 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: a client's HDMI vendor InfoFrame and dithering in a
 mode set of KAPI

Dolby Vision on NVIDIA goes out as nvidia-drm 615 lets a client send it: its
vendor InfoFrame (NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA), dithering off ("dithering mode")
and 8 bpc ("max bpc"). The 580 release, the one that drives Maxwell, Pascal
and Volta, has none of the three, and NVKMS here has no room for a client's
vendor InfoFrame or dithering in a mode set. Its ioctl API is shared with
NVIDIA's closed user space of the same release (libnvidia-eglcore,
libnvidia-allocator and libcuda open /dev/nvidia-modeset), so none of its
structures may change.

KAPI passes them with NVKMS_HADES_IOCTL_SET_MODE (nvkms-hades.h): the
NvKmsSetModeParams of NVKMS_IOCTL_SET_MODE followed by, for each head, the
client's vendor InfoFrame and its dithering. nvKmsIoctl() takes it from
kernel clients only, at its exact size, before its dispatch table; the
request goes to nvHadesSetDispModeEvo(), which nvSetDispModeEvo() now calls
with nothing added, so every other mode set (user space, the console) is as
before and leaves no client InfoFrame on a head it sets. KAPI's
KmsSetMode() always uses it, and a change of the InfoFrame, the dithering
or the depth is a mode set (ApplyModeSetConfig()), as on 615 where
InfoFrames are not flip-synchronized. The depth goes in the colorBpc that
the request already has.

The InfoFrame lives with the other InfoFrame state of the head. When it is
set it goes out every frame instead of NVKMS's own vendor InfoFrame, with
type 0x81, version 1, the length of the payload and the checksum, as 615's
SendVendorSpecificInfoFrame() sends it, through the same HAL
(nvEvo1SendHdmiInfoFrame(), the SendHdmiInfoFrame of nvEvo94 and nvEvo97,
the HALs of display classes 94/95 and 97/98: nvkms-hal.c, nvkms-evo2.c).
That HAL hands the HDR InfoFrame to the HDMI library as a vendor-specific
one too, into the same VSI slot of the SOR (NV9171_SF_HDMI_INFO_IDX_VSI, the
class that the library uses for GM10x to GP10x: nvhdmipkt.c), so while a
client's InfoFrame is set the HDR InfoFrame is not sent, the SDR one of an
HDR transition included, as 615 does without generic shared InfoFrames.

The mode set is refused, with the reason in the kernel log ("Hades: the HDMI
vendor InfoFrame of head N is refused: ..."), when the InfoFrame could not
be read as what it is: on anything but one HDMI display; and for the Dolby
OUI (46 D0 00) when it is not 27 bytes, asks for Low-Latency (PB4 bit 0:
this driver sends no YCbCr 4:2:2 AVI InfoFrame for it), or the output is
not the tunnel, 8-bit RGB 4:4:4 of full range without dithering, HDR
InfoFrame, BT.2100 colorimetry or output transfer function, in a mode that
needs no HDMI 1.4b vendor InfoFrame of NVKMS's own. Any other OUI (the HDMI
1.4b one that Kodi's 3D output sends, 00-0C-03) goes out as it is given.
The rules are on plain values in nvkms-hades.h.

The dithering of the head, when the client asks for one, replaces that of
the dpy in nvChooseDitheringEvo().
